7. We check each car. Once we approve it, it is on the lease at its tier and Home shows **Check and sign**: you sign the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Form B (the lease summary) in the owner portal, on screen (there is no paper option). Form D (the limited power of attorney) is in your Documents too: you sign it on screen with two witnesses beside you, and CarmaCars signs its Part 2 at the same moment.

> Good to know: Home and **Money** show **Your fleet lease**: each car, its tier, its lease a month and the next payment date. The lease is paid on the 10th for the month before, with your statement; the first payment comes at least one full month after the car goes on the lease, and part months are paid by the day. Add more cars from your owner portal the same way.',
  '<p class="gd-p">You apply online in about ten minutes. We reply within one business day, set your terms, and walk you through the rest.</p><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-apply-to-list-your-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Apply to list your car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Go to <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/list-your-car</span> and press <b class="gd-ui">Apply to list your car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Start with your name, mobile and email, and your car: its VIN, or its year, make and model. Press <b class="gd-ui">Continue</b>. From here every answer is saved as you type.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">About you: individual or corporation, your address, licence and date of birth. Press <b class="gd-ui">Continue to vehicles</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For each car, type the VIN: your car is found as you type the last character (Edit if anything is wrong), then tap its colour and answer the rest. Signed in? Press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> under Fill this from the ownership permit: the VIN, plate and colour fill in from a photo of your Ontario permit, for you to check. Use <b class="gd-ui">Add another vehicle</b> for more cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Read how it will work, press <b class="gd-ui">Continue</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit application</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Go to your owner portal</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/list-your-car</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/800"><img src="/guides/img/public-13-list-your-car-desktop-48bf4cb0.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="800"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.1%;top:74.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Need a break? Your answers are already saved. <b class="gd-ui">Email me a link</b> sends you a link to finish later, on any device. If you stop part way, we may email you a link to finish too.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>No car to add yet? On the vehicle step press <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ll add my car later</b>, choose your password and press <b class="gd-ui">Open my owner account</b>. Your owner portal opens with <b class="gd-ui">Add your first car</b>: press it when you are ready, starting with the VIN.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-what-happens-next" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What happens next</h2><p class="gd-p">Five steps take your car from your driveway to its first rental.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Tell us about the car</span><em>We confirm fees and set your terms</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Sign the agreements</span><em>Online, one for all your cars</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>One registry visit</span><em>We fill in the forms and come with you</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Tracker and insurance</span><em>We install it and add the car</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Photos and listing</span><em>Live within 1 business day</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Right after you apply, Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Read your agreements</b>: both agreements, filled in from your application, marked &quot;Terms pending approval&quot;. The fees and the Revenue Share read Pending approval until we set them, and the Sign button stays off.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When your terms are ready, Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b>. Everything is filled in from your application: check the short list of key values (each has a <b class="gd-ui">Fix</b> link) and open any document to read it in full.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sign in a few steps: say you read the documents, initial the three confirmations, tick the two consents and draw your signature. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Sign all</b>. A code to your phone or email is optional (<b class="gd-ui">Verify by code</b>); it is asked first only if CarmaCars turns it on. One signature covers every document, in about two minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Pay the upfront invoice: the first and last month&#39;s insurance fee for each car (see chapter 4).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Upload what each car&#39;s checklist asks for: the ownership permit, the lender&#39;s permission if it is financed or leased, and insurance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Sign Forms C and D (filled in for you) on screen, with your witnesses beside you on the same device: Form C with one witness, Form D with two (see chapter 5).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-if-we-need-a-little-more" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">If we need a little more</h2><p class="gd-p">Sometimes we need one more document before we can approve your application, for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">You get an email, and Home shows &quot;We need a little more&quot; with the list and any note from our team.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Upload what is asked, or write Your answer, and press <b class="gd-ui">Send my answer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">We review it within 1 business day. Once we approve your application, you get an email and Home shows Check and sign.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">No typing the VIN: press <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> and point your phone at the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield, or <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b> and take a photo of it. Check the VIN shown before you continue.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Photos:</b> on your car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> takes up to 30 at once, in any order. We sort them, put the outside photos on our studio background and keep the inside ones as taken. At least 10 are needed.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="apply-and-get-your-car-listed-a-fleet-supplier-lease-your-cars-to-carmacars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars</h2><p class="gd-p">For a corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars for a fixed amount a month. You pay CarmaCars no fees: no invoices, no debits.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Go to <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/list-your-car</span> and press <b class="gd-ui">A corporation with a fleet? Lease your cars to us as a fleet supplier</b> (or choose <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b> in the application, then <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: lease your cars to CarmaCars</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">About you: the corporation&#39;s legal name and number, its registered address, and the signing officer&#39;s name and title.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For each car: type the VIN (the year, make and model fill in), then the plate, and mark the car <b class="gd-ui">Regular</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Troubled</b> (it needs work). Each tier shows its lease a month. The tier is set when you add the car and does not change.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Say who the car is registered to now: <b class="gd-ui">My corporation</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Me or another officer, personally</b> (it moves into your corporation), or <b class="gd-ui">A seller: the corporation is buying it</b>. For the last two, enter the name and address on the ownership and the transfer or sale date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Continue</b>, check the review and press <b class="gd-ui">Submit application</b>. The ServiceOntario forms each car needs are filled in for you at once, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>: the lease to CarmaCars (CarmaCars holds the plates while it leases the car) and, for a car not yet registered to your corporation, the transfer into it. A seller signs the transfer on the back of the ownership. Only the empty boxes are filled; you sign them in ink at ServiceOntario.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">In your owner portal, open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then each car, and upload its ownership (registration) copy.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">We check each car. Once we approve it, it is on the lease at its tier and Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b>: you sign the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Form B (the lease summary) in the owner portal, on screen (there is no paper option). Form D (the limited power of attorney) is in your Documents too: you sign it on screen with two witnesses beside you, and CarmaCars signs its Part 2 at the same moment.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Home and <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> show <b class="gd-ui">Your fleet lease</b>: each car, its tier, its lease a month and the next payment date. The lease is paid on the 10th for the month before, with your statement; the first payment comes at least one full month after the car goes on the lease, and part months are paid by the day. Add more cars from your owner portal the same way.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'documents-and-forms', 'chapter', 'fees-payments-and-payouts', 'Your signed agreements, uploads and government forms are under Documents. Some forms are filled for you; Forms C and D are signed with witnesses.

## Sign everything at once

Everything you sign on screen is in one place: Home shows how many are signed ("2 of 5 signed") and opens it with Check and sign.

1. Press **Check and sign** on Home (or open `carmacars.ca/owner/sign`). The list at the top shows each document: signed, in this package, or done elsewhere (Forms C and D, the bank debit).
2. Check the key values: your name, address, each car with its VIN and plate, your fees and Revenue Share. Something wrong? Press **Fix** next to it, change it, and come back.
3. Open any document to read it word for word: the agreements, the schedules and Forms A and B. The official registry forms are not in it: they are printed and signed in ink.
4. A code is optional: press **Verify by code** if you want the certificate to say a 6-digit code to your phone or email confirmed it was you (it is asked first only if CarmaCars turns it on).
5. Tick that you read the documents, draw your initials in the box beside each confirmation the Enrollment Agreement asks for, and tick the two consents (to sign electronically, to get your records electronically).
6. Draw your signature in the box with your finger, a pen or the mouse, then press **Sign all**. One signature is applied to each document; CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment and every signed copy is in Documents.
7. Each signed copy ends with a certificate of completion: when and where each step was done, and whether a code confirmed it was you. Anyone holding a copy can check it at carmacars.ca/verify.

## Read your agreements before approval

You can read both agreements as soon as you apply, before we approve your terms.

1. Press **Read your agreements** on Home (Documents and each car''s Onboarding checklist link to it too).
2. Each document is filled in from your application: your name, address and cars. It is marked "Terms pending approval": the fees, the Revenue Share and the agreement numbers read Pending approval until we set them.
3. Something wrong? Press **Fix** next to it. The Sign button stays off until we approve your terms; then Home shows **Check and sign** and we email you.

> Two owners: A car with a second owner on its ownership? Each owner named in the Title Schedule signs. The other owner gets their own link by email and signs the same documents on their phone or computer, the same way: the documents read, the confirmations initialled, the consents and their drawn signature (a code to their email only if they choose it or CarmaCars turns it on). The agreements take effect when the last owner signs; CarmaCars countersigns then.

> Good to know: Cannot draw a signature (for example with a disability)? Call us: an Admin can let you type your name instead.

> Good to know: Form A (the trust declaration) is for cars under the Co-Registrant or Transfer method; Form B (the lease summary) for cars under a Lease method. No witness is needed: they are in the same package. You can also sign one on its own page from Documents.

> Tip: Signed one of your documents on paper instead? Send us the scan. Once we record it, Documents shows it as Signed on paper and we do not ask again.

## We set up your car for you

When our team enters your car for you, you get one email: review the details and sign.

1. No sign-in yet? The email has a link to choose your password. It works once, for 24 hours; after that use Forgot password on the sign-in page.
2. Open `carmacars.ca/owner/review` (Home has **Review or correct your details**). Check your phone and address, and each car: plate, colour, odometer, your insurer and your lender. The terms we agreed are shown too.
3. Something wrong? Correct it and press **Save corrections**. Your documents are filled in again and we are told. A term you did not agree to: message us before you sign.
4. Everything right? Press **Everything is right: sign** and sign once.

## Sign an updated Vehicle Schedule

When we agree new terms for a car you already signed for, you sign an updated Vehicle Schedule. Home shows it first.

1. Open it from Home or the email. It shows what changes (now and updated) and the date it applies from.
2. Read the text, then sign the same way as your agreements: tick that you read it, initial the updated terms, tick the two consents, draw your signature and press **Sign** (a code to your phone or email is optional).
3. Your current terms stay until you sign. After that, your invoices and statements use the new ones from the date. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, is in Documents.

## Form C on screen, with your witness beside you

Form C is the lender or lessor permission for a financed or leased car. It needs one witness, and you can sign it on screen when your witness is with you.

1. Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press Sign Form C on screen instead.
2. Tick that you read the form (a code to your phone or email is optional, unless CarmaCars turns it on).
3. Draw your initials beside each of the three acknowledgments, tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Hand the device to your witness, another adult. They type their full name and tick the statement "I witnessed (your name) sign in my presence." Press **Sign Form C**.

![](/guides/img/owner-16-form-c-screen-desktop-faa92983.jpg "desktop; size: 790 980; address: carmacars.ca/owner/documents/form-c/4898eb96-0cce-4efc-9fdd-740b4b4e9ad3; pins: 2 5.7 13.6, 3 32.9 55.1, 4 6.3 82.2")

## Forms C and D on paper, signed with witnesses

Form D is a limited power of attorney (two witnesses), signed on paper. Form C can be signed on paper too, with one witness.

1. Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press **Print the form**. It is filled in, and every spot to sign or initial is marked SIGN HERE or INITIAL HERE.
2. Sign it in front of your witnesses. They sign and print their names in their spots.
3. Type each witness''s full name in the boxes.
4. On your phone, press **Take a photo of the signed page**: one photo of each page. A PDF scan works too (**Or choose a file**).

![](/guides/img/owner-12-forms-c-d-desktop-21fbbe79.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 742; address: carmacars.ca/owner/documents; pins: 1 21.5 32.5, 3 69.4 50.7, 4 69.4 60.4")

> Tip: We check the photo and approve it, or send it back with what to fix. You get an email either way, and the page shows the status.

> Good to know: Why paper for Form D? It is a power of attorney, which cannot be signed electronically in Ontario, and its two witnesses sign in person.

## Government forms filled for you

Each car''s registry forms are prepared from your records, only the ones its onboarding method needs (013-1155 and 013-0169, for example, only for a Lease through a new corporation). Until we load the official PDF, you get a data sheet with the values.

1. Open Documents and choose a form marked "Official form, filled for you".
2. Press **Download the filled form** and check each value.
3. Print it and sign it in ink. It is the official ServiceOntario form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it, with only its empty text boxes filled in. Its boxes to tick and its signatures are done by hand, at the registry office or before you go, as we tell you.

![](/guides/img/owner-13-official-form-desktop-48614913.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 732; address: carmacars.ca/owner/documents/forms/4d54a524-c28d-4bc4-8ad3-dd9558100a81/official; pins: 2 22.2 29.5")

> Good to know: ON00453 (a company''s registrant number) is an Adobe form: open it in Adobe Acrobat Reader (free) to see and print it. Other PDF viewers show a blank page, as they do with the form downloaded from ServiceOntario.

> Watch out: Official registry forms are never signed on screen. You pay ServiceOntario, the inspection station and the appraiser directly.

## The agreement for your deal

Your agreement is filled in from the terms we agreed with you. We email you a link when it is ready: **Read and sign** opens it in your portal, and you sign once for every document.

1. **Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement**: if your corporation leases cars to CarmaCars. It lists each car with its tier (Regular or Troubled), its monthly lease and its delivery date. Each car''s tier is set once, when it is delivered. You pay CarmaCars no fees. We pay in arrears on the 10th: a car''s first payment comes one full month after delivery, and part months are paid by the day, with the calculation on your statement.
2. **Referral Override Agreement**: if you referred another owner. It sets the override we pay you on their cars (out of our share, never theirs) and what you can see of those cars. Find it under **Cars**: Sign your Referral Override Agreement.
3. Something wrong in it? Reply to the email before you sign and we fix it.
