  '<p class="gd-p">You give the renter the keys only after every check passes. The steps guide you one by one: press Next after each, Back to go back.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The job&#39;s header shows how much of the rental walkthrough the renter has read, for example &quot;Renter&#39;s walkthrough: read 2 of 6 steps&quot;. Below 6, walk them through the rest at the car: what to bring, the walk-around, the road rules and the return.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Finish the handover in the app, to the last step. Until the pickup is recorded the renter&#39;s messages and the office&#39;s records are guesses: 30 minutes after the pickup time you get an alert and a text to record it, or to mark a no-show.</div></aside><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-before-you-start-the-ready-check" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Before you start: the ready check</h2><p class="gd-p">The first step lists what must be done before the car can go: signed, paid, ID checked, deposit.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each line should show a green tick: agreement signed, identity verified, coverage confirmed, additional drivers accepted, the booking holds the calendar, deposit taken.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A red line shows what you can do about it right under it (see the next part). Fix it, then press <b class="gd-ui">Check again</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">All green? Press <b class="gd-ui">Next</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Coverage or the calendar not ready? Only the office fixes those: call CarmaCars. Still not ready? Press <b class="gd-ui">Stop: do not release the car</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/410"><img src="/guides/img/field-21-handover-01-ready-phone-ecb54c56.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="410"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:91%;top:63.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Never hand over keys if the ready check fails, the renter does not match the photo on file, or they do not have their original licence or the card on file. Stop and call us.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-fix-the-ready-check-on-the-spot" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fix the ready check on the spot</h2><p class="gd-p">Most red lines are fixed on your phone, without calling the office. Everything you do is recorded with your name.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Agreement not signed: press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b> and hand the phone to the renter. A copy signed on paper is not accepted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Identity not verified: for each driver, press <b class="gd-ui">Take</b> for the licence front, the back and the selfie. Hold the original licence: tick that the name matches, the photo is the person, it is valid past the return and it is class G2 or G. No expiry on file? Type the licence number and the expiry. Press <b class="gd-ui">The licence checks out</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Deposit not taken: press <b class="gd-ui">Card hold: hand this phone to the renter</b>. They type their card in Stripe&#39;s secure form; take the phone back and press <b class="gd-ui">Back to the job</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Paid by e-Transfer instead: open <b class="gd-ui">Paid by e-Transfer</b>, type the reference number from their confirmation and press <b class="gd-ui">Record the e-Transfer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Paid in cash: open <b class="gd-ui">Paid in cash</b>, count the amount in front of the renter and press <b class="gd-ui">I received</b>. Keep the cash apart from your own money and hand it to CarmaCars within 1 business day, as Finance directs: Finance gets a task to collect it from you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Additional driver not accepted: press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device (additional driver)</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An expired licence, a face that does not match or a renter who will not sign: do not fix it. Press Stop and call us.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-the-steps-one-by-one" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The steps, one by one</h2><div class="gd-phones"><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div>Car ready: fuel full or charged 80%, clean, extras in. <b class="gd-ui">Yes</b> or <b class="gd-ui">No</b>, with a note for Fleet.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-22-handover-02-car-ready-phone-c118e08b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div>Is this the renter? Compare the person with the name and photo on file.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-23-handover-03-renter-phone-813b8ced.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div>Original licence: name, photo and expiry match. A photo of a licence is not enough.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-24-handover-04-licence-phone-80a47254.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div>Card on File: you have seen the physical card with the same last four digits, in the renter&#39;s name.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-25-handover-05-card-phone-64652ced.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div>Odometer: type the reading in km.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-26-handover-06-odometer-phone-34c4cbd7.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div>Fuel or charge: tap the level on the gauge, in eighths from E to F.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-27-handover-07-fuel-phone-2df75f41.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div></div><div class="gd-phones"><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div>Keys: how many keys and fobs you hand over. Use <b class="gd-ui">+</b> and <b class="gd-ui">−</b>.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-28-handover-08-keys-phone-13bec781.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div>Photo set: 19 photos in order. Press <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> for the next one; every photo is also in the list below, with <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b> if needed.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-29-handover-09-photos-phone-767ecd4f.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div>Damage: tap the car diagram where it is, choose Where and Type, then <b class="gd-ui">Add the damage</b>.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-30-handover-10-damage-phone-a43b142f.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div>Tracker: it should say in place and reporting. <b class="gd-ui">Check again</b> if not. The car has to go anyway? Open <b class="gd-ui">The car has to go anyway?</b>, say why and press <b class="gd-ui">Release without the tracker</b>: an Admin is told at once.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-31-handover-11-tracker-phone-817976ce.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div>Renter reviews: the renter reads the summary of odometer, fuel, keys, photos and damage.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-32-handover-12-summary-phone-b1787a2d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div>Signatures: the renter signs, then you. <b class="gd-ui">Use this signature</b> for each.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-33-handover-13-signatures-phone-fac8ea8d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="13"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b>. You see &quot;Checked out. The rental has started.&quot; The renter gets the photo report by email and in their Documents.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Photos wait on the phone without a connection and upload by themselves when it returns; the count shows what is still uploading. Each photo keeps its time, and the place when your phone allows location. No signal on a step? It says &quot;Answers kept on this phone&quot; and you can go on: press Try again, or they are sent when the signal returns.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-sign-now-on-this-device" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign now on this device</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter (or an additional driver) has not signed the rental agreement yet? They sign on your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the job, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>. It shows who still has to sign and whether their licence is on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the person: the name matches their licence, and you saw the original licence. Tick both. No licence on file? Press <b class="gd-ui">Photograph: Licence, front</b> (and the back and the selfie).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> and their name. They read the agreements (CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s), tick the statements and sign with their name or their finger.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">They hand the phone back: press <b class="gd-ui">Back to the staff view</b>. The signature record says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your phone.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-the-agreements-at-check-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The agreements at check-out</h2><p class="gd-p">Both rental agreements follow the check-out.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Signing at pickup? Record the odometer and the fuel on the check-out first, then hand over the device: the agreement then shows the time, kilometres and fuel out, and the signed copy holds them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The signer gets a code on their phone, initials the key terms, ticks the consents and draws their signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Already signed online? When you complete the check-out, the &quot;as picked up&quot; copy of both agreements is made with your readings and your countersignature, and emailed to the renter.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The check-out stops if the agreement is missing something a claim needs (a licence expiry, a VIN). Ask the office to fill it on the booking, or an Admin to override.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-the-deposit-on-your-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The deposit on your phone</h2><p class="gd-p">Deposit not taken yet? The ready check shows how to take it under the Deposit line. You never type a card number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Card hold: hand this phone to the renter</b>. They type their credit card in Stripe&#39;s secure form and press the button with the amount.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They see &quot;Hold placed&quot;: take the phone back and press <b class="gd-ui">Back to the job</b>. The ready check shows the deposit taken.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A rental longer than the hold limit shows <b class="gd-ui">Save the card on this phone (long rental)</b> instead: Finance charges the deposit to that card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">No credit card? When CarmaCars allows it, the renter pays the deposit by e-Transfer or in cash: record it under the Deposit line.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-add-ons-to-put-in-the-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add-ons to put in the car</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking may come with add-ons: a baby seat, a child or booster seat, flowers, an umbrella, a phone charger or a prepaid full tank.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the job. Under Put in the car you see each add-on, how many, and what to do (for example &quot;Put the bouquet on the front passenger seat&quot;).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Put every item in the car before the handover. The Car ready step lists them again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Prepaid fuel: the renter may return the car at any fuel level. Do not charge for fuel at the return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A chauffeur on the booking: Fleet tells you who drives and when.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An item missing? Write it in the note for Fleet on the Car ready step and call the office before the handover.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The photo count shows &quot;19 of 19 photos taken · all uploaded&quot; when the set is complete. The first photo must show the plate. Open circles on the damage diagram were recorded before; add only what is new.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-on-one-screen-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">On one screen (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page the check-out is one screen: the time, km, fuel, and many photos picked at once from the camera roll, with the suggested angles as a checklist. If the renter checked in themselves, add your photos to theirs. The full checklist is still there when you want it.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('investor', 'start-here', 'start', null, '### Who this guide is for

Investors with an Investment Agreement with CarmaCars. Your portal shows each investment, what it has earned and paid, your monthly statements, and lets you send notices to us.

### What you need

- The invitation email from CarmaCars (investor accounts are by invitation only)
- Access to that inbox: the link works for 24 hours, once
- An authenticator app, if you choose two-step sign-in (recommended)

## Your first sign-in

1. Open the invitation email and press its link within 24 hours.
2. Choose a password of 8 characters or more and press **Save the new password**. You land on Home.
3. Next time, sign in at `carmacars.ca/sign-in`, or use Investor sign in at the bottom of any page of carmacars.ca.
4. Forgot your password? Press **Forgot your password?** on the sign-in page.

![](/guides/img/public-09-sign-in-phone-1f766061.jpg "phone; size: 390 645; pins: 3 95.4 78.4")

> Good to know: Link expired? The page it opens has **Send me a new link**.

## Stuck on a page?

If you spend a few minutes on a page without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks **Need a hand with** the page. **Open the guide section** opens this guide at the right chapter beside the page (a sheet from the bottom on a phone); **Back to what I was doing** closes it and everything you typed is still there. **Not now** quiets it on that page for a day. It never shows while you pay or sign.', 'Start here', 'Who this is for and your first sign-in.',
  '### Who this guide is for

Investors with an Investment Agreement with CarmaCars. Your portal shows each investment, what it has earned and paid, your monthly statements, and lets you send notices to us.

### What you need

- The invitation email from CarmaCars (investor accounts are by invitation only)
- Access to that inbox: the link works for 24 hours, once
- An authenticator app, if you choose two-step sign-in (recommended)

## Your first sign-in

1. Open the invitation email and press its link within 24 hours.
2. Choose a password of 8 characters or more and press **Save the new password**. You land on Home.
3. Next time, sign in at `carmacars.ca/sign-in`, or use Investor sign in at the bottom of any page of carmacars.ca.
4. Forgot your password? Press **Forgot your password?** on the sign-in page.

![](/guides/img/public-09-sign-in-phone-1f766061.jpg "phone; size: 390 645; pins: 3 95.4 78.4")

> Good to know: Link expired? The page it opens has **Send me a new link**.

## Stuck on a page?

If you spend a few minutes on a page without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks **Need a hand with** the page. **Open the guide section** opens this guide at the right chapter beside the page (a sheet from the bottom on a phone); **Back to what I was doing** closes it and everything you typed is still there. **Not now** quiets it on that page for a day. It never shows while you pay or sign.

> Good to know: When we update our terms of use, our privacy policy or an agreement you signed with us, the next time you open your portal it shows **We''ve updated our terms**: a short summary of what changed and the new text. Tick that you read it and press **Accept** to continue. It does not change an agreement you already signed or a past booking.',
  '<h3 class="gd-h3">Who this guide is for</h3><p class="gd-p">Investors with an Investment Agreement with CarmaCars. Your portal shows each investment, what it has earned and paid, your monthly statements, and lets you send notices to us.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">What you need</h3><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The invitation email from CarmaCars (investor accounts are by invitation only)</li><li>Access to that inbox: the link works for 24 hours, once</li><li>An authenticator app, if you choose two-step sign-in (recommended)</li></ul><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-your-first-sign-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your first sign-in</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the invitation email and press its link within 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a password of 8 characters or more and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the new password</b>. You land on Home.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Next time, sign in at <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/sign-in</span>, or use Investor sign in at the bottom of any page of carmacars.ca.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Forgot your password? Press <b class="gd-ui">Forgot your password?</b> on the sign-in page.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/645"><img src="/guides/img/public-09-sign-in-phone-1f766061.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="645"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.4%;top:78.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Link expired? The page it opens has <b class="gd-ui">Send me a new link</b>.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-stuck-on-a-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Stuck on a page?</h2><p class="gd-p">If you spend a few minutes on a page without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks <b class="gd-ui">Need a hand with</b> the page. <b class="gd-ui">Open the guide section</b> opens this guide at the right chapter beside the page (a sheet from the bottom on a phone); <b class="gd-ui">Back to what I was doing</b> closes it and everything you typed is still there. <b class="gd-ui">Not now</b> quiets it on that page for a day. It never shows while you pay or sign.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>When we update our terms of use, our privacy policy or an agreement you signed with us, the next time you open your portal it shows <b class="gd-ui">We&#39;ve updated our terms</b>: a short summary of what changed and the new text. Tick that you read it and press <b class="gd-ui">Accept</b> to continue. It does not change an agreement you already signed or a past booking.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('investor', 'your-investments', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'Home shows what needs you first (a document to sign, a notice, a return on hold), then each of your investments: what you put in, what it earns, and when it pays.

## Read an investment

1. The menu: **Home**, **Live sheets**, **Documents** (with the tabs **Statements**, **Documents to sign** and **Your files**), **Investor deck** (while CarmaCars shares it) and **Account**. **Guide** and **Sign out** are at the top.
2. Your agreement number and name, your Invested Amount, the Returns paid to date (or reinvested) and the next payment, with a chart of your account month by month.
3. Each investment: its Invested Amount, how far the lockup period has run, the Yearly Percentage, how Returns are handled (Paid monthly or Reinvested) and the Next Payment Date. Principal, what was reinvested and redeemed to date, the Investment Date and the Lockup End Date are under "Principal, dates and amounts to date".
4. Payment schedule: the last Returns on your statements and the next ones. An amount that is not on a statement yet is marked Estimated.
5. Latest statement, with **Open**.

![](/guides/img/investor-01-investments-phone-16342025.jpg "phone; size: 390 1605; pins: 1 25.6 15.3, 2 38.5 34.9, 3 51.3 72.6, 5 51.3 95.0")

> Tip: This area shows your records under your Investment Agreement. It is not an offer or a solicitation.

## Live sheets

**Live sheets** is the CarmaCars investment workbook on the website, filled in from your own records. It updates itself: when a payment to you is recorded, it shows as Paid on your next visit.

1. **My investment**: your Invested Amount, start date, Yearly Percentage, lockup end, the payouts made so far and the next payout with its date. Below is your schedule: your statements as recorded (Paid, To be paid, On hold, Reinvested), then the months ahead (Projected). Switch **Paid monthly** or **Reinvested** to compare the months ahead; it does not change your choice (that is a request under Account).
2. **Calculator**: type an amount (at least the minimum), a start date and a yearly percentage, and choose Paid monthly or Reinvested. You see the monthly payout, when the lockup ends, the first payment, what is paid by months 24 and 36, and the 36-month schedule. It starts from your own numbers.
3. **How it works**: the terms in plain words, step by step, with examples.
4. **Fund a car**: for buying a car and placing it in the owner program. Type the price, the daily rate, the days you expect it rented and the terms of your owner agreement. You see your monthly payout, the yearly figures, the return on the car and the payout schedule. Add up to three cars.
5. **Download as Excel** gives you the same sheets as a spreadsheet with working formulas, with your numbers filled in. **Download as PDF** gives your investment, your schedule and how it works on a few pages.

> Tip: The sheets show only your own records and the investment terms. The months ahead are estimates; your monthly statement is the record.

## Sign your investment agreement

When CarmaCars sends your agreement, it is under Documents, Documents to sign, and first on Home.

1. Press **Read and sign** on Home, or open **Documents** > **Documents to sign**. The top shows what is signed ("0 of 1 signed").
2. Check the key values: your name and address, the Invested Amount, the Yearly Percentage and the dates. The agreement is filled in from your record.
3. Press **Read the PDF** and read it, with its schedules.
4. Say whether you got independent legal advice.
5. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the risk acknowledgment (Schedule C), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
6. Press **Sign**. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, is on the same page.

Once you sign, the agreement shows "Awaiting countersignature by CarmaCars" under Signed. CarmaCars''s signing officer countersigns it; the agreement binds CarmaCars once it is countersigned and your funds have cleared. You get the countersigned copy on the same page.

> Tip: Signed on paper instead? Once we record it, it shows under Signed with the scan.
